I bought the same version back then as the OP bought now. It is as you
guessed: The disk label only seems to refer to the publishers (PC-SIG)
numbering. It is v1.1 of Title #1000 (appropriately decent number for
this wonderful game) of their software library.

The version *really* included is Nethack 2.3f. I had to dig around my
older disks and reattach an old 5 1/4" drive to be sure. Amazingly,
no problems whatsoever to read the entire disk. The files are packed
inside a self-extracting archive.

The date of the newest game files is 15.09.1988. But I think I bought
my copy in 1991. Can't remember seeing it much later.

