Maybe this *is* the book, the OP writes about. In fact: Although this
Public Domain game was sold for about 20 DM, it *didn't* include any
printed documentation. Just the disk inside a paper sleeve, the folded
paper containing the blue front and back pages, which the OP linked to.
And a plastic wrapping. 

To be honest: I'm not the least bit disappointed for having billed 
this seemingly high price. It was reasonable - compared to other means 
for getting new software. Only disk swapping was noticeably cheaper.
Although my first updates to Nethack were free of charge, monetarily,
they cost me much, much more. I remember sitting about a day on an
Internet computer, watching the bytes drop in one-by-one from one of
the free Ftp servers...

> *Jedi* Knights must be a misunderstanding of the normal Knight, right? 

No. Version 2.3f really had a Jedi class with a light sword. Nice
weapon. But you had to attach new batteries when the power went low.
And you could get it from bones, of course. I liked starting with
Ninja (sometimes over 60 shuriken) and picking up a light sword and
some batteries on one of the first levels. Got me usually farthest.
;-)

